  "vfx": {
    "Piece": {
      "Note": "pieces/celestial_dragon: the spirit dragon as two skinned GLBs. DragonBody.glb: the body (DragonBody, a SurfaceAppearance of translucent blue scales, AlphaMode Transparency), its ForceField sheath, Neon core and Neon flame fins, on the bones Dragon (root, still) and Spine1-30, each a Path motion riding the swimming loop Swim (piece.json Paths: a lap round the cue, tip end to butt end and back, in 10 s) with two Bobs on top (a quick wave down the body) and on Spine1 a tail flick. DragonHead.glb: the generated head as a hologram with its ForceField shell, on Head (riding Spine30: nods, looks round, rears back roaring every 4.8 s), Jaw (gapes on the roar) and Mane. Every joint is Aura (hidden on the shooter's turn); piece.json has each pivot and motion, and each Bone's Transform is set as the report says (6.3).",
      "Triangles": 20536
    },
    "Moving": {
      "Kind": "Piece + Orbiters + emissive",
      "Note": "Energy flows through the dragon's body: four Orbiters ride its exact coil (from the butt to the shaft in 2.4 s, turning -1.333 turns a second so they follow the 3.2-turn helix, their radius measured from the cue's surface) with bright trails and glowing heads, two per ribbon, half a lap apart; star dust shimmers round it; the head breathes and roars (the piece motion); the cue's emissive (the sapphires and the star gem) breathes 1.4-2.2."
    },
    "Aura": {
      "Note": "A spirit dragon of blue light swims round the cue (the 3D piece): it circles the cue all the time while it slithers from the tip end to the butt end and back, turning round at each end (a lap in 10 s; its snout never closer than a few inches to the tip), its body following the path its head swam with a quick wave running down it, its tail flicking, its head looking round and rearing back to roar; blue spirit flames peel off its back and head and trail behind it; drifting star dust (four-point stars twinkling in and out, white to blue); soft blue light motes; a soft blue glow round the cue (a halo Beam, breathing) and a blue light on the cue. The dragon is aura: it goes with the rest on the shooter's turn.",
